From b01ccb40dae362f6c0cc5af5683086d5adf06637 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:10:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Video engine quality + reliability overhaul
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Quality (all deterministic ffmpeg, no new AI cost):
- Real music ducking: narration loudness-normalized (-16 LUFS), music
  sidechain-compressed under speech and swelling back in pauses (was a
  static 0.2 volume), final mix normalized to the -14 LUFS platforms expect
- Stock scenes seek INTO long clips (golden-ratio spread, deterministic)
  instead of always replaying from t=0; short clips still loop
- Dip-to-black fades on topic-video scene cuts (was hard concat cuts)
- Slideshows: cover-crop + gentle alternating Ken Burns zoom on a 2x
  supersampled frame (was static letterboxed stills with black bars)
- Raw AI clips normalized to the REQUESTED aspect/resolution (WAN outputs
  720p, MiniMax ignores aspect, Veo is 16:9-first) — fail-soft passthrough
- Poster frames: 1080px grabbed past the fade-in (was 640px at 0.5s)

Reliability:
- Replicate create/download wrapped in bounded retry-with-backoff on
  429/5xx/network; polling tolerates 3 consecutive transient failures
- TTS calls bounded by a 90s timeout + one retry, so a hung narration
  can never stall a 25-minute topic video
- New retry.ts helper with typed transient-status detection

UI: expose the Pexels/Pixabay footage-source choice the backend already
supported (was hardcoded 'auto').

Tests: 5 new (real-ffmpeg normalize, fail-soft passthrough, retry/timeout
semantics); all 43 videoGen tests green including upstream topicVideo and
character-scene suites against the new filter graphs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EJdoZ8bk1pWTrmbMVQJZ7G
